  "limitations": [
    "FlagsFirst is an explicit qualified CPU profile, not an assertion of identical competing-fault order on every x86 CPU",
    "canonical IRET encodings beginning in 64-bit mode; compatibility return stops at the existing privilege-return boundary",
    "complete legacy i386 dispatch and task gates, SMI/software SMM, SGX enclave/AEX/EPCM remain open",
    "REP/gather/XSAVE partial completion, intra-instruction async events, LOCK, MMIO, TLB and concurrent writers remain separate",
    "CET/FRED/LAM/LASS and later TF execution require their own owners; native LA57 unavailable on this host",
    "no LLVM or NeverC source change required for this runtime lowering; final LLVM release and pin intentionally remain pending"
  ],
